{
  "source": "nodejs-sdk@c0ff3fd packages/core/src/sse/parser.test.ts; docs/product-spec/13-server-sent-events-and-streaming.md (the chapter's conformance fixtures)",
  "note": "Each case is the whole input of one stream and the events a reader must produce, in order. input is UTF-8 text with \\r, \\n, \\u0000 and \\ufeff escapes; inputHex replaces it where the bytes are not valid text. The over-cap retry cases are re-derived for the int.MaxValue ms cap this port documents (Node caps at Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER). The line-cap cases are .NET's and live in the Security tests, not here (Node has no default cap). Ruby's SSE test paths did not exist at ruby-sdk@fa402cd, so no case is ported from them.",
